# Known-good git subcommands for the enforce-git-dash-c hook.
# One subcommand name per line; blank lines and #-comments are ignored.
# A git invocation whose subcommand is not on this list is blocked outright,
# regardless of whether -C is present or would be auto-corrected - extend
# this file when a new subcommand is legitimately required by the workflow,
# rather than changing hook logic.
#
# NOTE: being listed here only means "the subcommand itself is permitted".
# config keeps its own read/write policy (check_config_call) and worktree
# keeps its own add/non-add split (block-git-worktree) on top of this gate.

add
am
branch
checkout
cherry-pick
clone
commit
config
diff
fetch
log
ls-remote
merge
mv
pull
push
rebase
remote
reset
restore
rev-list
rev-parse
revert
rm
show
stash
status
switch
tag
worktree
